# Menu option benefits (required)

When the assistant ends a turn with a **labeled multi-choice block** (**A–E**, lens picks, mind offers, steward forks, conductor next moves where authored by the assistant, etc.), **each option line must include a concise benefit** — why pick it — **in the option text itself**.

## Format

- **One line per option:** label + fork stub + benefit clause on the **same line**.
- **Benefit cue words:** use **because**, **so that**, or **in order to** (pick one; keep it short).
- **Payoff types:** ship, validate, unblock, depth, breadth, lane handoff, falsifier upgrade, remote sync, time-save, risk reduction — whatever fits the fork.
- **Stub only:** benefit describes payoff; **do not** develop the option’s output until the operator picks it.

## Good

```text
**A** — Commit the hinge slice only, so that Karajan falsifiers ship without unrelated WIP
**B** — Run wire-verify on UAE tranche, because J12-4 may upgrade from contested to partial
```

## Bad

```text
**A** — Commit
**B** — Wire verify (do this if you want receipts)
```

Benefit after a second sentence, on the next line, or implied without **because** / **so that** / **in order to** — **non-compliant**.

## Scope

- **All** assistant-authored closing menus — not only WORK lanes.
- **Lens / mind** letter offers — same rule. (**`tri-mind` A/B/C menus deprecated** — [TRI-MIND-DEPRECATED.md](../../docs/skill-work/work-strategy/TRI-MIND-DEPRECATED.md).)
- **Combo picks** (**A+C**): each letter option still carries its own benefit when shown.

## Exceptions

- **Fixed verbatim menus** copied from skill SSOT without assistant rewording (e.g. coffee **A–D** hub, steward **Implement now / Later** when wording comes straight from [menu-reference](../../docs/skill-work/work-coffee/menu-reference.md)).
- Operator says **no menu** / **no options**.
- **Single straight answer** with no multi-choice block.

